(5638181, 817980, 77192, '<td valign="top">That looks delicious!<br/> <br/>When I first saw this I wasn''t sure about it, as the crust of the bread seemed a bit sharp and the blurring around the edge of the chopping board seemed too soft. But on second glance I think the two cause each other. i.e. it''s only the sharpness on the bread that makes the board seem too soft and vice versa. On balance I think it looks about right.<br/> <br/>The scene looks very natural, and not at all staged. Ironically I bet it takes real effort to make it seem so effortless lol.<br/> <br/>The colurs are perfectly vibrant and not all over-saturated. In short, this is my favourite shot of the challenge so far. Oh go on, have a 10 ;-)<br/> <br/>Edit: I was worried about submitting a "recipe" shot for this challenge. I came to the conclusion that pasta''s one of those foods that doesn''t photograph well, looking sometimes like it was sort of thrown on the plate. Your shot proved me wrong :-) That said, my shot does look thrown on the plate and is scoring accordingly. If you''ve got a moment, would you mind having a look at my shot when voting is finished and telling me what you think? I''ve got a lot to learn about food photography, although it is one of my favourite sort of shots. Thanks a lot :-)</td>', 'That looks delicious! When I first saw this I wasn''t sure about it, as the crust of the bread seemed a bit sharp and the blurring around the edge of the chopping board seemed too soft. But on second glance I think the two cause each other. i.e. it''s only the sharpness on the bread that makes the board seem too soft and vice versa. On balance I think it looks about right. The scene looks very natural, and not at all staged. Ironically I bet it takes real effort to make it seem so effortless lol. The colurs are perfectly vibrant and not all over-saturated. In short, this is my favourite shot of the challenge so far. Oh go on, have a 10 ;-) Edit: I was worried about submitting a "recipe" shot for this challenge. I came to the conclusion that pasta''s one of those foods that doesn''t photograph well, looking sometimes like it was sort of thrown on the plate. Your shot proved me wrong :-) That said, my shot does look thrown on the plate and is scoring accordingly. If you''ve got a moment, would you mind having a look at my shot when voting is finished and telling me what you think? I''ve got a lot to learn about food photography, although it is one of my favourite sort of shots. Thanks a lot :-)', '2009-09-06 18:06:07.000000', NULL, 1),
