(5638988, 818020, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i>People should double dog dare you more often! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No thanks. Whenever I''m "expected" to come through, I pull out all the stops. So tournaments, DPL, direct competitions and topics that I suggest account for the vast majority of my higher scores. I don''t have IreneM''s grasp of color and composition, the models of Kiwiness or Librodo, or the landscapes of Iceland or Cannon Beach, so I have to lean heavily on concepts. It''s tough to do that on every single challenge, so I''ve generally avoided the DPC Olympics, Formula competition and side challenges. Plus, I''m down to one camera with a sticky shutter button. :-(<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-09-07 11:54:42.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN:People should double dog dare you more often!  No thanks. Whenever I''m "expected" to come through, I pull out all the stops. So tournaments, DPL, direct competitions and topics that I suggest account for the vast majority of my higher scores. I don''t have IreneM''s grasp of color and composition, the models of Kiwiness or Librodo, or the landscapes of Iceland or Cannon Beach, so I have to lean heavily on concepts. It''s tough to do that on every single challenge, so I''ve generally avoided the DPC Olympics, Formula competition and side challenges. Plus, I''m down to one camera with a sticky shutter button. :-(', '2009-09-07 12:21:53.000000', '2009-09-07 12:54:42.000000', 0),
