(5642181, 817114, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/> You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.  <br/> <br/>Ohh come on, how am I supposed to give an in depth comment to something that is brilliantly thought out, planned, executed??????<br/> <br/>You are sharp, clean, clarity is spot on, the colours that you chose work well. <br/> <br/>Excellent work!!!</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club,  You asked for your shot to have an in depth comment from a member of the Critique Club.   Ohh come on, how am I supposed to give an in depth comment to something that is brilliantly thought out, planned, executed?????? You are sharp, clean, clarity is spot on, the colours that you chose work well.  Excellent work!!!', '2009-09-09 15:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5642425, 818020, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scalvert:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i>People should double dog dare you more often! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No thanks. Whenever I''m "expected" to come through, I pull out all the stops. So tournaments, DPL, direct competitions and topics that I suggest account for the vast majority of my higher scores. I don''t have IreneM''s grasp of color and composition, the models of Kiwiness or Librodo, or the landscapes of Iceland or Cannon Beach, so I have to lean heavily on concepts. It''s tough to do that on every single challenge, so I''ve generally avoided the DPC Olympics, Formula competition and side challenges. Plus, I''m down to one camera with a sticky shutter button. :-( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You should avoid free studies too. :P</td>', 'Originally posted by scalvert: Originally posted by JulietNN:People should double dog dare you more often!  No thanks. Whenever I''m "expected" to come through, I pull out all the stops. So tournaments, DPL, direct competitions and topics that I suggest account for the vast majority of my higher scores. I don''t have IreneM''s grasp of color and composition, the models of Kiwiness or Librodo, or the landscapes of Iceland or Cannon Beach, so I have to lean heavily on concepts. It''s tough to do that on every single challenge, so I''ve generally avoided the DPC Olympics, Formula competition and side challenges. Plus, I''m down to one camera with a sticky shutter button. :-(   You should avoid free studies too. :P', '2009-09-09 19:35:52.000000', NULL, 0),
